      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Dan Sheehan's no8 run worked for Leinster, but Foley doubts a repeat",
          "body": "Leinster's experiment with Ireland hooker Dan Sheehan at no8 against Munster worked, and Sheehan made the most carries of any player, 17. Irish Mirror columnist Derek Foley doubts Leinster will repeat it. Foley points to the no8's control of five-metre scrums, a job Leinster gave to Jamison Gibson-Park, and to Sheehan's limits as a lineout jumper and defensive option. With Caelan Doris, Jack Conan and Josh Ericson injured, Leinster were short of back-row options, Foley notes."
        },
