      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Derby form",
          "heading": "Wales wing Josh Adams scores as Cardiff shut out Ospreys 26-0",
          "body": "Wales wing Josh Adams was released from the national squad to play for Cardiff in Saturday's Welsh derby, and he scored in a 26-0 win at St Helen's. Released to get much-needed minutes, the 31-year-old had played just twice this season. Cardiff's red-zone defence did the damage, keeping the Ospreys off the scoresheet for the first time in over two years. Adams's score came from a grubber by centre Steff Emanuel, who was involved in all three first-half tries."
        },
