          "heading": "Harry McLaughlin-Phillips shines as Australia A beat USA 52-0 in New Jersey",
          "body": "Australia A completed a clean sweep of the USA with a 52-0 win over the Eagles in New Jersey, and the standout was Harry McLaughlin-Phillips, who scored a try, piled on 17 points and set up at least three others. Several Wallabies hopefuls stood up, with Mac Grealy, name-dropped by coach Les Kiss over the weekend, among the backs with five-pointers and three line breaks. Zac Lomax, playing his first international match, improved as the game went on. The Eagles never scored, trailing 33-0 at the break."
